{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_018: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted fusion → 52.3% acc). With a single data point, the most critical uncertainty is whether the RNA modality actually contributes to performance or whether the image alone accounts for most of the signal. Question: config_004 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean ablation of config_018 with only the RNA modality removed, isolating the effect of multimodality. Why this is the best next experiment: Without an image-only baseline, we cannot interpret any future multimodal result—improvements could come from better image features, RNA contribution, or fusion interactions. Establishing this reference point first ensures that all subsequent experiments (varying RNA encoder, image encoder, aggregation, fusion) are interpreted against a meaningful unimodal floor. It is a single-variable change, maximally informative, and essential before investing budget in more complex multimodal variants."
}

